(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[12 1 "// The import system (PY5e; PYI-SPEC.md §9's single-file imports): import-name, import-from and"] [13 1 "// import-star, and builtins.__import__, after importlib._bootstrap's __import__, _gcd_import,"] [14 1 "// _find_and_load and _handle_fromlist. A module is found on sys.path (a package's submodules on its"] [15 1 "// __path__): DIR/NAME/__init__.py (a package), DIR/NAME.py, else DIR/NAME as a namespace package; its"] [16 1 "// source is compiled to the IR by the host (SetCompiler: the reader and arbace.python.compile) and run"] [17 1 "// as the module's body. The built-in modules are builtins and sys; the C modules of CPython are PY6's"] [18 1 "// Go ports (survey §6.6), so their import is a ModuleNotFoundError until then. importlib._bootstrap as"] [19 1 "// the import system itself (PYS12) is PY6's: no finders, loaders or specs yet (__spec__ is None)."] [21 1 "// builtinModuleNames are sys.builtin_module_names: every module the runtime makes (builtinModules', builtinModulesErr's),"] [22 1 "// with sys and builtins, sorted. Computed at first use, after every file's init registered its modules (PY6-core, queue"] [23 1 "// 200: a fixed list here missed the families' new modules, and importlib's BuiltinImporter then did not find them)."] [32 31 "// loaded on their first import (builtins_pyexpat_api.go)"] [43 1 "// builtinModules make the built-in modules other than builtins and sys, once per interpreter (their files'"] [44 1 "// init functions fill it: _string's builtins_string.go, _weakref's builtins_weakref.go)."] [47 1 "// builtinModulesErr are the built-in modules whose making may raise (those that run Python's machinery:"] [48 1 "// _ast's classes through type())."] [51 1 "// compileHook compiles a module's source text to the IR's text (arbace.python/ir-text); mode is \"exec\""] [52 1 "// or \"single\" (the REPL's). Any other result than a code object's map is an error \"Type: message\", or"] [53 1 "// \"incomplete\" for an interactive statement that needs more lines."] [56 1 "// SetCompiler sets the host's compiler of Python source (bin/pyi's host, arbace.python.run)."] [59 1 "// compilerLimitError is the compiler's answer for a source nested past its limits (queue 289): the parser's"] [60 1 "// MemoryError (pegen's MAXSTACK) or the compiler's RecursionError, as CPython raises them; else nil."] [73 1 "// compileSource compiles source text by the host's compiler into a code object."] [106 1 "// syntaxError is the SyntaxError (IndentationError, TabError) of the compiler's answer"] [107 1 "// \"MSG\\x00LINE\\x00OFFSET\\x00END_LINE\\x00END_OFFSET\\x00KIND[\\x00TEXT]\" (the location's parts empty when unknown; KIND m"] [108 1 "// is p with \"\\x00STMT_LINE\\x00STMT_COL\" before the text, the exception's _metadata with the source): its"] [109 1 "// fields filename, lineno, offset, text, end_lineno and end_offset, as CPython's compile() raises it. The text: a"] [110 1 "// parser's error (KIND p) the line as the parser gives it (TEXT, None when absent); a compiler's (KIND c) the line"] [111 1 "// of the file when it reads (PyErr_ProgramTextObject: None for \"<string>\"); an answer of no kind the source's line."] [127 18 "// err_programtext: the first line's BOM skipped (queue 223)"] [137 2 "// kind m (queue 202c): a parser's error with its _metadata, the last statement's line and column"] [138 2 "// (_PyPegen_set_syntax_error_metadata), then the text as kind p's"] [152 4 "// _PyErr_ProgramDecodedTextObject: the line decoded by the file's encoding, errors replaced (queue 223)"] [183 1 "// readerField undoes the prefix's escapes of its separators (arbace.repr.python.astjson's prefix-field)."] [186 1 "// emitReaderWarnings emits the reader's warnings ahead of a compiler's answer (arbace.repr.python.astjson's"] [187 1 "// warnings-prefix: for each \\x01 and its category, message, line, then the error it becomes, class, message, line,"] [188 1 "// offset, end line, end offset, text, joined by \\x02; then \\x03) and gives the answer: PyErr_WarnExplicitObject at"] [189 1 "// the warning's line, a warning a filter turns into an error the reader's SyntaxError (_PyTokenizer_parser_warn,"] [190 1 "// warn_invalid_escape_sequence: the parse ends there, queue 228)."] [223 4 "// _PyPegen_number_token: a decimal literal over sys.set_int_max_str_digits's limit, which is the run's: the"] [224 4 "// reader records the digits of one past the lowest limit (p[1]) and the error's location"] [234 21 "// a compiler's warning: PyErr_ProgramTextObject's line"] [245 1 "// compileModuleName is 3.15's compile(..., module=NAME) while that compile runs (nil: none): the warnings' module"] [246 1 "// (_PyErr_EmitSyntaxWarning's PyErr_WarnExplicitObject(..., module, NULL); queue 239)"] [249 1 "// emitCompileWarnings is _PyErr_EmitSyntaxWarning for each of the compiler's warnings, in order:"] [250 1 "// warnings.warn_explicit(msg, SyntaxWarning, file, line); a SyntaxWarning a filter turns into an error becomes"] [251 1 "// the SyntaxError of its location, the compile's result."] [297 1 "// isIncomplete reports an interactive statement that needs more lines (codeop's incomplete input):"] [298 1 "// (PY7: a fresh _IncompleteInputError each time, isIncomplete tells it)"] [314 4 "// 3.15 (queue 239): _PyEval_LazyImportName, unless the compiler forced the import eager"] [349 1 "// eagerImportName is IMPORT_NAME's eager import (_PyEval_ImportName): builtins.__import__ called, or the runtime's."] [352 3 "// builtins.__import__ replaced: called as CPython's import_name calls it"] [373 4 "// a mapping's namespace (a dict subclass's, exec's mapping; queue 219): the names stored through it"] [387 1 "// builtinImportFn is the runtime's builtins.__import__."] [390 1 "// isBuiltinImport is whether o is the runtime's builtins.__import__."] [393 1 "// builtinImport is __import__(name, globals=None, locals=None, fromlist=(), level=0)."] [432 1 "// importName is IMPORT_NAME (importlib's __import__): the module named, relative to globals' package by"] [433 1 "// level; with an empty fromlist the top-level package of the name, else the module with fromlist's"] [434 1 "// submodules imported."] [457 3 "// import_ensure_initialized: a module another thread is still initializing is waited for, by its module lock"] [458 3 "// (_bootstrap._lock_unlock_module); 3.15 only here (queue 239: lazy imports reified by threads at once)"] [477 3 "// PyImport_ImportModuleLevelObject: an imported module's pending registration on its parent settled (3.15)"] [522 1 "// handleFromlist imports the submodules a package's fromlist names (_handle_fromlist)."] [555 5 "// _handle_fromlist: a missing submodule is skipped, unless sys.modules blocks it with None"] [566 1 "// importFrom is IMPORT_FROM: module.name, else the submodule module.name already in sys.modules (a"] [567 1 "// circular import), else an ImportError."] [569 2 "// PyObject_GetOptionalAttr: a lazy import's pending submodule by its name (suppress; 3.15, queue 239)"] [600 3 "// import_from's shadowing messages (ceval.c, queue 223): the spec's file origin, else __file__"] [610 4 "// PySet_Contains(sys.stdlib_module_names, mod_name): __name__ itself, a str subclass's hash (queue 250)"] [634 2 "// import_from's ImportError: name the module, path its file, name_from the name (PY6b's request)"] [643 1 "// importStar is IMPORT_STAR: __all__'s names, else the module's public names, into ns."] [692 1 "// packageOf is the package a relative import is relative to (import.c's resolve_name, _calc___package__):"] [693 1 "// __package__, checked against __spec__.parent; else __spec__.parent; else, with an ImportWarning, __name__"] [694 1 "// (itself for a package)."] [754 1 "// resolveName is _resolve_name: name relative to package by level."] [770 1 "// importModule is _gcd_import: the module of the absolute name, its parents imported first."] [778 2 "// importlib's _find_spec at shutdown: finalize_modules set sys.meta_path to None (queue 253)"] [789 4 "// 3.15's _bootstrap calls _imp._set_lazy_attributes after a load (queue 239)"] [852 1 "// importBuiltin makes the built-in module name and puts it in sys.modules (ok false when name is not one):"] [853 1 "// the runtime's own import of them, and _imp.create_builtin's under importlib (PY6b)."] [863 23 "// a module whose Go package the host loads on demand (pyexpat)"] [866 25 "// PY6d's R5: the built-in functions' __module__"] [882 1 "// findAndLoad finds the module child (fully name) in the directories of search and runs it."] [918 1 "// loadSource compiles a module's source file and runs it as name (a package when path is not nil)."] [931 32 "// 3.15 no longer sets __cached__"] [970 1 "// notFound is ModuleNotFoundError(msg) for the module name (its .name, ImportError's attribute)."] [990 1 "// moduleDict is a module's namespace (a *Module's Dict), else nil."] [1003 1 "// moduleName is a module's __name__, \"\" when it has none."] [1019 1 "// modulePath is a module's __path__ (a package's), nil for a plain module."] [1035 1 "// The runtime's import system seen by importlib (PY6a): sys.meta_path holds pyiFinder, whose find_spec imports"] [1036 1 "// the module by the runtime's own finder (sys.path, packages, the built-in modules) and answers a"] [1037 1 "// ModuleSpec of importlib._bootstrap whose loader hands that module over, so importlib.import_module and"] [1038 1 "// importlib.util.find_spec work beside the import statement. importlib._bootstrap as the import system itself"] [1039 1 "// is the import family's (PY6)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[96 33] [116 39] [123 28] [124 24] [150 33] [153 27] [154 41] [225 33] [231 112] [232 30] [276 126] [277 29] [279 36] [332 37] [351 43] [375 31] [379 70] [404 26] [450 46] [461 42] [463 34] [464 61] [465 55] [476 25] [479 39] [480 47] [515 52] [547 41] [553 37] [554 29] [556 44] [579 56] [589 27] [590 47] [596 55] [604 48] [612 37] [613 25] [618 47] [677 4] [685 25] [716 83] [734